---
/* The homepage shell.

   The pin-and-scrub smoke test that lived here is gone, as the spec
   and START-HERE both require: it existed to prove the scroll
   infrastructure end to end, and it has done that.

   The four real sections — hero, bird, people, services — land here
   one at a time under the SDD loop. Nothing below is final content.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="bKash — Financial freedom for millions"
  description="A secure digital account where millions store value and decide how to use it."
  current="home"
>
  <main class="shell">
    <div class="wrap shell__in">
      <p class="t-eyebrow">Foundation</p>
      <h1 class="t-display">Financial freedom for millions</h1>
      <p class="t-lead">
        The shell is built: tokens, fonts, nav and footer. The hero, the bird, the people and
        the services sections land here one at a time.
      </p>
      <p class="t-body">
        Every label in the nav and the footer is placeholder until bKash approves it, and the
        page is <code>noindex</code> until the content is signed off.
      </p>
      <p class="t-sm shell__link">
        <a href="/specimen">Token specimen</a> · <a href="/about">About shell</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  /* Clears the fixed header from the single source, --nav-h. Audit
     X2: the prototype's sections sat under the header because the
     offset existed nowhere. */
  .shell {
    padding-top: calc(var(--nav-h) + var(--s-8));
    padding-bottom: var(--s-10);
  }

  .shell__in > * + * {
    margin-top: var(--s-4);
  }

  .shell__link {
    margin-top: var(--s-6);
  }

  code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
</style>
